    const-string v131, "Antimatter is regular matter with all the electrical charges inverted. However! Neutrinos have no electrical charge whatsoever. Therefore, scientists theorised, neutrinos might be antiparticles of themselves! But although neutrinos are common, collision is rare because neutrinos are extremely, extremely small, and even if some did collide, we would have almost no way of detecting without extensive scientific research and equipment, so we have yet to know the true answer... Wait... What? Uh... Yeah? Lepton charge? Oh well. Screw it, here\'s the latest news flash."

