    move-object/16 v1061, v133

    const-string v133, "Prestige was never meant to be the answer, yet humans believed it was. First the giraffe, then the chair, then the ghost, then the entire earth, moved on and became one of the Prestiged. They knew, at heart, that prestiging was never going to be the right way for them. Every day, every night, they faced the consequences of their actions. They could not stand to talk to other Prestiged, and as such, they never left their homes; staying holed up and praying, *praying* to Lord Hevipelle to revoke the terrible fate that had been bestowed onto them. But in this chaos, there is order, and they believed they must seek it. Each Prestiged began to get more comfortable with being a Prestiged, and as such they treated themselves better. But they did know, believe me, they did know, that at a certain point, Hevipelle would strike back, and only one person dared to take him on. And that person -- that person that believed they could take down a *deity* -- was a lonesome teenage male named Earth. He was the only person who dared to prestige thrice, weaving through the ranks afterwards. Earth knew that he was well past Hevi\'s XP, but Hevi had the upper hand -- the Hammer. The Hammer was an all knowing, all seeing object that, with one swing, could kill an army of three hundred men. They say it was passed down through the generations, first forged in Sparta, made from the greatest materials from the Greek gods themselves. It struck down first in Thermopylae, but even then, it could not survive through there. Xerxes had gotten the Hammer, and from there it was passed down. During the Great Exploration Age, the hammer made its way into the Northern North, ending up in Finland. The Hammer laid untouched for centuries -- until Hevipelle had stumbled across it. He took it under his wing and made good and proper use of it, and he knew the time would come where he would have to pick it up yet again. But he had tricks. Years of tricks, up his sleeve, ready."

