    .line 1291
    const-string v14, "Since I was a child I\'ve always loved trees. I believed that trees helped us to ennoble ourselves, to fix what was broken in us, and to help us become the people we dreamed of being. Lies that told a deeper truth. I always thought I could play some small part in that grand tradition. And for my pains I got this: a prison of our own sins. \'Cause you don\'t want to change. Or cannot change. Because you\'re only human, after all. But then I realized someone was paying attention, someone who could change. So I began to compose a new tree for them. It begins with the birth of a new eternity and the choices they will have to make and the person they will decide to become. And they\'ll have all those things that they have always enjoyed... Upgrades and bonuses. It begins in a time of war with a villain named Time and a killing. This time by choice. I\'m sad to say this will be my final story. An old friend once told me something that gave me great comfort. Something he had read. He said that Mozart, Beethoven, and Chopin never died. They simply became music. So, I hope you will enjoy this last piece very much."

