    move-object/16 v1156, v130

    move-object/16 v1153, v130

    const-string v130, "What does it mean to be a game developer? It means lying. Boldly, and brazenly to your audience. Promising them release dates that are wildly outside the realm of reality. And when that promised release date has turned out to be a lie, you double down even harder on the next wildly unrealistic release schedule. Don\'t worry you tell them, this is the one for sure. Round and round the cycle goes. Is there any video game in development at all? Who can say anymore? The lies have become the game itself. A promise indistinguishable from reality. Anyway, the game has been content complete since 2018 and we were just waiting for a parable about flat stanley to release a second time to release reality. April fools! Wait, we missed that release date didn\'t we?"

