    move-object/16 v1211, v130

    const-string v130, "In the last ever congress of young mathemantics, a game was played out to test if computers could think. 1400 delegates agreed to a \"pure\" game where they could only execute certain rules, and communicate with one\'s and zeroes. As time passed and hours went by, the delegates became increasingly confused, annoyed, paranoid. Some became dizzy and lost track of the rules, some made up responses and entirely ignored the rules, and some collapsed on the floor, to be taken to rest and recover. After a day, it was revealed the game was an attempt to translate a specific phrase from a language no delegate knew, to a language very close to heart. The translation was known, having been done by a computer following the exact same rules hours earlier. But due to the human nature of the individual bits and bytes being simulated, the human\'s translation was wrong. Although the computer translated \"The greatest goals are achieved through minor but continuous efforts.\", the humans translated \"The greatest goals are achieved through minor but continuous worship.\" Upon discovering these results, the congress was never held again."

