    const-string v132, "A traveler stepped into a bar. \"Excuse me, what time is it? It\'s not 5 o\'clock, right?\" \"Ha, are you an outsider? No, take a seat. It\'s not 5 o\'clock, it\'s already seven.\" \"Then why...\" \"You see that big clock outside, standing in the center? No, it\'s not a clock, it\'s a countdown, an anticlock if you will.\" \"Anticlock? So this universe is named.\" \"We are famous? Then you believed those ridiculous stories, huh?\" The local tippler sulked. \"We are so beautifully designed, living in amazing dimensions, one producing lower ones? Ha, that\'s only a jail built by our so-called lord.\" \"Excuse me? What I heard is...\" \"Look at that clock again, I said it is an Anticlock, but it doesn\'t even count down.\" 04:59:59 04:59:59 04:59:59 \"The lord, Hevipelle, promised to wipe out the potential monsters such as...eh what\'s it called? Oh...ninth dimension, and promised to build a whole new reality for us, then he disappeared! Leaving us doing the same job day after day. He said he will come back when the Anticlock is done! But the clock got stuck when it counted down to five hours. Nothing can fix it, and our life, our world has been abandoned!\" 04:59:59 04:59:59 04:59:59 \"I see...I was thinking 5 hours was just a joke in this colorful universe...\" \"No, it\'s not your fault. Our world did produce something good to attract travelers like you to visit. Sorry to reveal our hopeless truth to you.\" The local tippler gave a cup of drink, \"Here, have a drink, young man.\" The traveler took the drink, \"I was curious about more stories about your lord and that so-called Anticlock...Wait?\" 04:59:58 04:59:57 04:59:56"

