    move-object/16 v718, v129

    const-string v129, "My grandfather lived and died doing what he \"loved\"; writing books. He wasn\'t really a successful writer and hadn\'t published any of his books. Except these books weren\'t like any you usually read. While we were cleaning his home, I found a key that led to an abnormally large basement. There, he stored thousands, if not tens of thousands of books. It\'s like as if he wanted to make his own personal library. I had to grab one of his \"books\" from a random shelf. But it turned out to be a few hundred pages of just random numbers. I grabbed another and to my surprise, it has the same contents as the previous. After checking out at least fifty different books, I started to question his motives. And that curiosity turned into regret, as I really never asked gramps about his career in writing. As soon as I wanted to leave, I discovered one book that stood out from all others. The cover had the number one on it. And in the first page, it read: \"I have denied the one true God, the one unlike any religion we have in our world. This being doesn\'t see us as ants, but as words. I am forever cursed to write down its unfathomable wealth. A currency not shaped like a piece of metal, rather... subatomic.\". After reading what I assume was the only piece of literature he truly made, a revelation hit me. In all the myriad books he had written, he hadn\'t even finished a fraction of what IT wanted him to make."

