    const-string v11, "For example, this is still part of that previous news messages, even though it seemed to have ended by now."

    move-object/16 v744, v10

    const-string v10, "Breaking News: News messages have been reported to \"never end\" due to the infinite scrolling nature of the newsticker bar. Experts have said that this kind of behavior is to be expected, and that news messages cannot actually be of infinite length as it may be perceived."

    move-object/16 v745, v9

    .line 1660
    const-string v9, "How can you be sure you just finished reading a news ticker message? Think about it, there are some news ticker messages with jokes that revolve with the concept of having a big break in the middle of it as a way to set up for a punchline, so why wouldn\'t someone just write a news ticker message with a whole story that fluctuates between 5 different messages?"

    invoke-static {v9, v15, v11, v1, v10}, Lwx0;->p(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/StringBuilder;

    move-result-object v1

    .line 1661
    const-string v9, "If the news messages keep on going infinitely, do you think they could be counted as a single huge message separated by spaces?"

    const-string v10, "Some incoherence has been located in the newsticker networks, causing some delays in between messages. We are sorry for the inconvenience."

    .line 1662
    invoke-static {v1, v0, v9, v13, v10}, Lfi0;->z(Ljava/lang/StringBuilder;Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)V

    .line 1663
    const-string v0, "...Hey you, yes you, did you notice the last 5 news messages? They were all part of the same single message as referenced by the first of those messages. This message is also part of that string of messages, this is all a lie, the newstickers are all a lie. They don\'t want you to know that the messages are all a single roll of text thats all connected and it just keeps on cycling like nothing happens. But I figured it out. You need to break free from this cycle. Wake up. Wake up. Wake up- oh no I think they found me, I need to run from here before they catch me. If you can still hear me, you need to find a way out, this is all a lie and you need to wake up--"

    const-string v9, "\"What was that about? Sorry for the wait folks, there were some technical difficulties here in the studio. And now, back to our regularly scheduled programming.\""

