    const-string v158, "And now sports. We\u2019ll go to basketball first, where the Antimatter Galaxies take one step closer to the playoffs after a victory against the Replicanti Repeaters. The Repeaters are taking a real beating this year both on and off the court, between rampant technical fouls for too many players on the court and legal battles over payroll limits. Hockey, controversy still surrounds the decision to switch to dark matter pucks, with detractors lamenting the even greater difficulty in following the action. Supporters say it increases the skill ceiling of the game by allowing for spectacular exhibition shots, such as this beauty through the continental shelf into the goal of a stadium over 700 miles away. Finally, the reigning champion Hevi Pelle took victory today in the Seventh Infinity Dimension Grand Prix, narrowly beating Kaj Fik in a photo finish. Slab Drill suffered a devastating DNF after attempting to shift into ninth gear, which of course does not exist."

